WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.900
What AD CS holds up.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.263
It isn't one server.

3
00:00:03.263 --> 00:00:06.071
The typical estate is
a two-tier hierarchy:

4
00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:10.645
an offline standalone root that signs
the issuing CAs and its own CRL,

5
00:00:10.645 --> 00:00:16.101
and enterprise issuing CAs that issue from
templates stored in Active Directory.

6
00:00:16.101 --> 00:00:21.718
Every enterprise CA also lives as objects
in the forest's Public Key Services

7
00:00:21.718 --> 00:00:27.950
branch: certificate templates, enrollment
services, the NTAuth certificates object,

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.725
AIA and CDP containers, key
recovery agents and OIDs.

9
00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:37.600
Those objects are forest-wide, which is
exactly what ties AD CS to Active Directory.

10
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.669
Domain members enroll through Group Policy
autoenrollment, which runs every eight

11
00:00:42.669 --> 00:00:47.375
hours and renews a certificate after it
passes eighty percent of its validity.

12
00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:50.820
Chapter 02's inventory
has four layers: the CAs,

13
00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.625
the templates, the issued
certificates and the relying parties.

14
00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:59.039
The relying-party layer decides
the order of work later,

15
00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:03.937
because a new issuer is useful only once
everything that validates it trusts it.

16
00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:08.838
Then every template and use case gets
one of four verdicts, asked in order.

17
00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:11.788
RETIRE first, if the
consumer is going away.

18
00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:17.117
MIGRATE, if Cloud PKI through
Intune or Entra CBA replaces it:

19
00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:21.275
Wi-Fi, VPN, device
authentication, tenant sign-in.

20
00:01:21.275 --> 00:01:26.351
BRIDGE, if it depends on AD itself
or a server the cloud can't reach:

21
00:01:26.351 --> 00:01:30.087
domain controllers, LDAPS,
NPS and NTAuth trust.

22
00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:33.584
RETAIN is what's left, such
as HSM-held code signing,

23
00:01:33.584 --> 00:01:36.825
and every entry gets an
owner and a review date.

24
00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:40.456
Appendix B applies these
verdicts template by template;

25
00:01:40.456 --> 00:01:42.460
we'll come back to it in Module 4.
